{
    "article_summary": "This article describes a photoredox-mediated nucleophilic (radio)fluorination of TEMPO-derived alkoxyamines. The method utilizes a radical-polar crossover mechanism where mesolytic cleavage of alkoxyamine radical cations generates carbocations that are trapped by [18F]fluoride. The protocol is mild, redox-neutral, and compatible with a wide range of functional groups, enabling the synthesis of secondary and tertiary alkyl fluorides that are difficult to access via traditional SN2 pathways. The process was successfully automated on a commercial radiosynthesis platform for clinical applications.",
